    <tok fileIndex="0" linenr="627" column="1" str="/*x * formatf() - the general printf function.x *x * It calls parsefmt() to parse the format string. It populates two arrays;x * one that describes the input arguments and one that describes a number ofx * output segments.x *x * On success, the input array describes the type of all arguments and theirx * values.x *x * The function then iterates over the output segments and outputs them onex * by one until done. Using the appropriate input arguments (if any).x *x * All output is sent to the &apos;stream()&apos; callback, one byte at a time.x */"/>
